{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TT-PHALYX Save Bank\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Saves the complete parameter and FX state of TT-PHALYX to one of 8 bank slots. Requires the TT-PHALYX Drum Sampler JSFX to be installed.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 TT-303 ACID MACHINE \u8212- mono acid synth in the style of the TB-303. Tribute, no samples, no sample ROM, all model.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 CONTROLS AS ON THE ORIGINAL TUNING semitones (-24..+24), plus FINE in cents CUTOFF filter frequency, ~150 Hz .. ~2 kHz exponential (rises with resonance) RESONANCE feedback of the 18 dB ladder up to self-oscillation ENV MOD depth of the filter envelope, up to 5.2 octaves DECAY decay of the filter envelope, ~30 ms .. ~570 ms ACCENT level AND filter boost of the accent circuit WAVEFORM sawtooth / square\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MODEL DETAILS (after R. Whittle / Devil Fish documentation)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Filter: 3-pole ladder (18 dB/oct) in ZDF/TPT form, level-dependent feedback k/(1+0.4|y|), 2x oversampled, then 3-point decimation. Soft clip only at the master, never in the OS loop (it never engages there at real levels anyway).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Pole correction 1/(1+0.10*kRes): mild peak correction; the resonance hump moves up with rising resonance, as on the reference.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Feedback HP 20 Hz IN the feedback path (DC block).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Square with frequency-dependent duty + tilt, classic 1-sample PolyBLEP.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Accent capacitor: recharge +0.95, saturation 1.65. Accent sweep with non-linearity and slight cutoff dependency.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab On accent: fixed 0.2 s filter decay + shortened VCA attack (1.8 ms).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Slide: constant time, log frequency space; the same note stays held.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab FX: delay/reverb bypassed at mix < 0.5 %. EQ OFF = true bypass.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab MIDI: notes are consumed, CC/pitchbend keep going.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 OPERATING MODES HOST Pure sound generator, played from the piano roll. Velocity >= threshold = accent, overlapping notes = slide. SEQ Internal 16-step sequencer, four pattern banks A-D with copy function, random and mutation, shuffle, gate length. Runs on the project timeline or free (FREE RUN). MIDI notes transpose the pattern (C2 = original pitch). MIDI OUT also sends the sequence out. All four banks travel with the project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Effect path: ahead of each of the three units \u8212- WaveShaper (Soft/Hard/ Fold/Fuzz), ping-pong delay, Freeverb reverb \u8212- sits an input EQ as a dual slider (lowcut left, highcut right, 0..20 kHz). After that compressor (-14 dB, 5:1) and master.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The input EQ only shapes what is sent into each effect; the dry signal runs alongside untouched. On the drive what the EQ removes is added back after the WaveShaper, so a raised lowcut takes the bass out of the DISTORTION, not out of the output (drive off = transparent).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIDI: THRU at the top of the header passes INCOMING notes on to the output (CC and pitchbend always pass through anyway). SEQ OUT in the sequencer panel sends the SELF-GENERATED sequence out. Two different sources, hence two switches. In SEQ mode incoming notes are transpose commands \u8212- whoever also passes them on with THRU sends them out next to the sequence.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 SURFACE after the Tim Techlor design kit: Core Black, Core White, Acid Green #39FF14, traces at a 45 degree angle with solder pads. Wordmark in Zilap Orian, if installed. Labels sans-serif (Segoe UI / Helvetica Neue / DejaVu Sans / Arial), numeric values monospaced (Consolas / DejaVu Sans Mono / Menlo / Courier New). Which of these is present the script measures itself. The front computes in a fixed design grid and scales to the window size \u8212- to enlarge, just drag the FX window open. HiDPI is honoured via gfx_ext_retina. All internal JSFX sliders are hidden ("-" before the name), operation is exclusively via the device front.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 TT-PHALYX Drum Sampler v1.03\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 16-pad sample player for Reaper with the feature depth of Vengeance Phalanx, in the Tim-Techlor design (sibling of the TT-303 Acid Machine). Triggering is MIDI only - no internal sequencer.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == THE FRONT == Top: 16 slim pads. Click selects the pad, M = mute, S = solo, the fader sets the pad volume, the LED shows active voices. Center: the full panel of the selected pad. A/B chooses the slot the two knob rows act on (transpose, fine, gain, start, rnd offset, delay, LPF/HPF/LoFi/Spike). A -> B copies slot A to slot B, PHASE inverts, REV plays backwards, SCR arms the scratcher. The fader below mixes A and B (crossfade). Right: the INPUT box - KIT note (kit mode, channel 1) or MIDI channel 1-16 (multitrack, tonal with keytrack - base = ROOT), killnote (choke), voices, one-shot vs sustain, envelopes -> init, PB range.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == LOADING A KIT == The front has no file dialogs. Load a kit with the Lua script "TT-PHALYX Load Kit.lua" (Actions -> Load ReaScript): pick any WAV from the kit folder - the folder is sorted across the 16 pads (entries 1-16 = sample A pads P01-P16, 17-32 = sample B) and written to tt-phalyx-kit.bin, which the FX adopts automatically every ~0.5 s. tt-phalyx-kit.txt is the readable reference. Kit mode listens on channel 1 and uses the GM map (36 kick, 38 snare, 42/46 hats, 41/45/48 toms, ...).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == THE TABS == AMP Amp envelope over the waveform (drag the points), timescale, retrig keytrack/fade, one-shot/sustain. FILTER Type (LP/HP/BP/notch, 6/12/24 dB), cutoff, reso, env mod with draggable filter ADSR, drive clean/dirty. PITCH Pitch envelope (drag the points), range in semitones, step quantise, flip; portamento OFF/POLY/LEGATO. FX Master chain: 4-band EQ (band type per click +1 / R-click -1, live response curve) -> 4 insert slots (each type + 4 parameters + mix): DELAY, CHORUS, FLANGER, PHASER, DISTORT, CRUSH, COMP, LIMIT, ROOM, TRASH, GATE, STEREO. LOOP Loop editor of the selected slot: LOOP on/off, drag the start/end flags, NRM/PING/XFD, ZERO (zero-crossing search against clicks), XFADE length. MOD Mod matrix 8 rows (click source > target, drag amount; sources VEL/KEY/G1-G3/M-X/M-Y/LFO1/LFO2/MENV/RND, targets VOL/PAN/PITCH/CUTOFF/RESO/LFO1/2-RATE/XFADE), 2 LFOs, mod envelope, velocity depth + curve with sketch, panorama per slot, GUI modifiers G1-G3. MIDI/ARP Drum kit matrix: click a key to assign it to the pad. Right: the arpeggiator - mode (R-click back), shuffle (drag the number = swing), octaves +/-, rate, gate. Modes UP/DOWN/UP-DN/RND/ROLL (ROLL = retrigger wall, e.g. for hat rolls). SYSTEM Readouts, interpolation LIN/AA (anti-alias Hermite, more CPU but cleaner upshifting), IN TRANSPOSE +/-24 st (in kit mode remaps the whole kit - like Phalanx), POLYPHONY 4-64, SNAP/UNDO, BANKS B1-B8 (load), SYNC (tempo sync: delay time and/or arp rate follow the project tempo - delay 1/16 to 1/1, arp 1/4 to 1/32).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == SCRATCHER == Arm the pad with the SCR button, hold a note, grab the waveform and drag - the playhead of both slots follows the position. The same position is automation slider 53 (MIDI learn/modulator).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == BANKS & UNDO == A bank stores ALL pad parameters plus the FX chain; samples come from the kit. Saving: Lua script "TT-PHALYX Save Bank.lua" (asks for slot 1-8, writes tt-phalyx-bankN.bin). Loading: B1-B8 in the SYSTEM tab. UNDO restores the pad's last state; a snapshot is also taken automatically on every pad switch.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == MIDI LEARN == All parameters sit as hidden automation sliders 1-63 behind the front: 3-52 mirror the selected pad, 53-63 scratch/system/arp/ root/PB/shuffle/sync; the FX knobs in the FX tab are separate. Learn as usual via Reaper (Param -> MIDI learn / modulator).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 == LIMITS VS. PHALANX == 1 stereo output (Phalanx: 16 - workaround: multiple instances), 64 voices global (1-16 per pad), no convolution reverbs, bank saving via Lua (JSFX file access is read-only), undo is one level per pad.\par}
}

